<v Host>It is said to have begun in seventeen thirty-three, during the Edo period.

00:07:26.175 --> 00:07:46.791
<v Host>That's all for today. The Sumida River Fireworks Festival, one of Tokyo's most famous summer traditions, returns on Saturday, July twenty-fifth, with about twenty thousand fireworks over two venues, carrying on a history said to reach back nearly three hundred years. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

